  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "The number of basic land cards you put onto the battlefield is equal to the number of lands you control when Boundless Realms begins resolving.",
      "oracle_id": "e6acafb7-856f-4125-a908-a620635b8ba3",
      "published_at": "2012-07-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For Kyoshi Island Plaza's first ability, the number of Shrines you control is checked when the ability resolves. You will still search and shuffle your library if you control no Shrines when the ability resolves, but you won't get any lands.",
      "oracle_id": "c0cdc333-6c5a-401c-9810-220d2027f2fe",
      "published_at": "2025-10-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The colors are white, blue, black, red, and green. Colorless is not a color.",
      "oracle_id": "27a3aa64-1de7-4b0c-af23-52886e7d258a",
      "published_at": "2025-11-17",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The effect of Prismatic Undercurrents's last ability is cumulative with similar effects. For example, if you control two Prismatic Undercurrents, you'll be able to play three lands during each of your turns.",
      "oracle_id": "27a3aa64-1de7-4b0c-af23-52886e7d258a",
      "published_at": "2025-11-17",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The value of X is calculated only once, as Prismatic Undercurrents's first ability resolves.",
      "oracle_id": "27a3aa64-1de7-4b0c-af23-52886e7d258a",
      "published_at": "2025-11-17",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Lands are normally colorless permanents, even if they tap for mana of a certain color.",
      "oracle_id": "27a3aa64-1de7-4b0c-af23-52886e7d258a",
      "published_at": "2025-11-17",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If no players control at least two more lands than you when the ability resolves, you'll still search and shuffle your library.",
      "oracle_id": "9633730d-c41f-4597-b806-55ce2dd848e9",
      "published_at": "2013-10-17",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You count the number of players who control at least two more lands than you when the ability resolves.",
      "oracle_id": "9633730d-c41f-4597-b806-55ce2dd848e9",
      "published_at": "2013-10-17",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you choose to find only one basic land card, you put it onto the battlefield tapped.",
      "oracle_id": "8b755881-a72d-4e21-a369-d2924eb4585a",
      "published_at": "2010-08-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can get just one basic land card if you wish (or even none at all). If you get only one land card, you put it onto the battlefield tapped.",
      "oracle_id": "1593ea18-2f2f-4ab4-83fb-6ccc0bec8a90",
      "published_at": "2004-12-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The land does not count toward your one per turn limit because it was put onto the battlefield by an effect.",
      "oracle_id": "8539f295-5d58-4436-a73a-b9277c4c7795",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you don't have a commander, Command Tower's ability produces no mana.",
      "oracle_id": "0895c9b7-ae7d-4bb3-af17-3b75deb50a25",
      "published_at": "2020-11-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you have two commanders, the ability adds one mana of any color in their combined color identities.",
      "oracle_id": "0895c9b7-ae7d-4bb3-af17-3b75deb50a25",
      "published_at": "2020-11-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If your commander is a card that has no colors in its color identity, Command Tower's ability produces no mana. It doesn't produce {C}.",
      "oracle_id": "0895c9b7-ae7d-4bb3-af17-3b75deb50a25",
      "published_at": "2020-11-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For effects that check whether a player searched a library or may search a library, searching the top four cards of that library counts as searching that library.",
      "oracle_id": "d9517c5d-66d0-4178-96fb-a8c04f311ad8",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "After the search is complete, the entire library is shuffled.",
      "oracle_id": "d9517c5d-66d0-4178-96fb-a8c04f311ad8",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each search works exactly the same as normal except that the opponent doing the searching sees only the top four cards of that library. They can't look at the other cards in that library at all. Cards not in the top four cards of the library can't be found in the search, even if they're identifiable in some manner.",
      "oracle_id": "d9517c5d-66d0-4178-96fb-a8c04f311ad8",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect uses the word \"search\" once but allows an opponent to search for multiple cards, the top four cards remain the same throughout the entire search. Finding one card won't cause the fifth card to become included in the search.",
      "oracle_id": "d9517c5d-66d0-4178-96fb-a8c04f311ad8",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The only difference between a colored artifact and a colorless artifact is, obviously, its color. Unlike most artifacts, a colored artifact requires colored mana to cast. Also unlike most artifacts, a colored artifact has a color in all zones. It will interact with cards that care about color. Other than that, a colored artifact behaves just like any other artifact. It will interact as normal with any card that cares about artifacts, such as Shatter or Arcbound Ravager.",
      "oracle_id": "5794b58e-f3b6-4637-b288-283b3a72a718",
      "published_at": "2008-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect says \"Search your library . . . then shuffle your library,\" you shuffle you libraries even though you can't search.",
      "oracle_id": "5794b58e-f3b6-4637-b288-283b3a72a718",
      "published_at": "2008-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Effects that instruct you to reveal or look at cards from the top of you library will still work. Only effects that use the word \"search\" are affected.",
      "oracle_id": "5794b58e-f3b6-4637-b288-283b3a72a718",
      "published_at": "2008-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect says \"You may search your library . . . If you do, shuffle your library\" or \"You may search your library . . . then shuffle your library,\" you can't choose to search, so you won't shuffle.",
      "oracle_id": "5794b58e-f3b6-4637-b288-283b3a72a718",
      "published_at": "2008-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Archelos's abilities don't apply to itself as it enters the battlefield, nor do they apply to any permanents entering the battlefield at the same time.",
      "oracle_id": "fd19a009-d1ab-4148-a829-3d4c3af1b0b2",
      "published_at": "2020-11-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If more than one Archelos is on the battlefield, the controller of an entering permanent chooses how to order the replacement effects.",
      "oracle_id": "fd19a009-d1ab-4148-a829-3d4c3af1b0b2",
      "published_at": "2020-11-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If another replacement effect says that a permanent enters the battlefield tapped while Archelos is untapped, the entering permanent's controller chooses whether the permanent enters tapped or untapped. If a permanent is simply put onto the battlefield tapped without a replacement effect being applied, it always enters untapped if Archelos is untapped.",
      "oracle_id": "fd19a009-d1ab-4148-a829-3d4c3af1b0b2",
      "published_at": "2020-11-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If there are fewer than twenty cards in the targeted player's library, that player puts all the cards from their library into their graveyard.",
      "oracle_id": "cc2b6e58-2d6f-495e-95f3-9496105c4cba",
      "published_at": "2009-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat.",
      "oracle_id": "8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90",
      "published_at": "2012-07-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
